{
  "id": 522324265,
  "iid": 26254,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "PROFINET: Add secure SXP SAM and SCM dissection",
  "description": "Add PROFINET 2.50 Security Association Management and Security Configuration Management decoding for SXP.\n\nDecode current SAM and SCM request and response blocks while preserving the legacy security block handlers `dissect_SecurityRequest_block()`/`dissect_SecurityResponse_block()`. Those will be removed in a future PR when the specification is finished. Add DevID domain, certificate, certification path, CSR, security capability, and configuration parameter fields.\n\nCorrect the ARAlgorithmInfoBlock and ExpectedCredentialTypeBlock layouts. Bound all current security block members by their declared lengths so malformed input cannot consume subsequent blocks.\n\nDecode the secure SXP wrapper according to IEC 61784-6-3. Expose SecurityMetaData and SecurityChecksum for authentication-only packets, then pass the plain SXP packet data through normal service reassembly. Preserve authenticated-encryption payloads as bounded opaque SecurityData.\n\nAlso update PNIOStatus mappings for SXP, RTAv3, PNIOSEC, and legacy protocol-machine values. Add PRAL alarm item and AR record access policy block dissection, refresh record indexes and IOCRProperties, and correct DCP and SXP display labels.\n\nValidated the changes with a secure SXP capture and repository API checks.\n\nAI-Assisted: yes \\[GitHub Copilot\\]",
